{
  "_doc": "INDEPENDENT ANALYTIC REFERENCE points for reprojection/lambert_conformal.esm -- the reprojection analogue of an MMS reference solution, NOT a binding-produced golden and NOT a shadow evaluator of any ESM document. Every value below was computed directly from Snyder (1987, USGS PP 1395, pp. 104-110) spherical Lambert Conformal Conic closed-form equations in double precision (Python math): forward eqs. 14-1 (x = rho sin theta), 14-2 (y = rho_0 - rho cos theta), 14-4 (theta = n (lambda - lambda_0)), 15-1 (rho = R F / tan^n(pi/4 + phi/2), rho_0 at phi_0), 15-2 (F = cos phi_1 tan^n(pi/4 + phi_1/2) / n), 15-3 (n = ln(cos phi_1/cos phi_2) / ln(tan(pi/4 + phi_2/2)/tan(pi/4 + phi_1/2))); inverse eqs. 14-9 (lambda = lambda_0 + theta/n), 14-10 (rho = sign(n) sqrt(x^2 + (rho_0 - y)^2)), 14-11 (theta = atan2(x, rho_0 - y), n > 0), 15-5 (phi = 2 atan((R F/rho)^(1/n)) - pi/2). Implementation verification: (a) reproduces Snyder's own numerical example (pp. 295-296: lat_1=33, lat_2=45, lat_0=23, lon_0=-96, R=1, point (-75, 35) -> n=0.6304777, F=1.9550002, rho_0=1.5071429, x=0.2966785, y=0.2462112) to all published digits; (b) reproduces the independent proj4/Snyder gold points embedded in archive/reprojection/lambert_conformal_conformance_test.jl (WRF lat_0=38.999996/R=6370000 and NEI2016 R=6370997 parameter sets) to <= 9e-15 relative. pyproj was not importable in the ESS venv at authoring time, so the archive proj4-derived points served as the external cross-check.",
